    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d248">

                <pb facs="0641" n="527" xml:id="pg527"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">Roosevelt Papers: Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The President’s Chief of Staff</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">Leahy</hi>) <hi
                        rendition="#italic">to the Assistant to the President’s Military Aide</hi>
                        (<hi rendition="#italic">Hammond</hi>)</head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">secret</hi>
                    </seg>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">[<placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps">Birch
                                Island, Ontario</hi></placeName>,] <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1943-08-02">August 2, 1943</date>.</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>
                    
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Black</hi>
                     8. Transmit following message to the Prime Minister, the Combined
                    Chiefs of Staff and the Secretary of State: <quote rend="blockquote">
                        <p>“I have read instrument of surrender<anchor n="1" xml:id="d248-f1"/> and
                            while the language seems on the whole good, I seriously doubt
                            advisability of using it at all. After all, the terms of surrender
                            already approved and sent to Eisenhower<anchor n="2" xml:id="d248-f2"/>
                            ought to be all that is necessary. Why tie his hands by an instrument
                            that may be oversufficient or insufficient? Why not let him act to meet
                            situations as they arise? Signed Roosevelt.”</p>
                    </quote>
                </p>
                <p>Add the following sentence just before signature in the message to the Prime
                    Minister only: <quote rend="blockquote">
                        <p>“You and I can discuss this matter at 
                                <hi rendition="#small-caps">Quadrant</hi>.”<anchor n="3"
                                xml:id="d248-f3"/>
                        </p>
                    </quote>
                </p>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d248-f1" n="1" xml:id="d248-f1-content">
                <p>Although the British Joint Staff Mission at Washington had circulated a new draft
                    of “long” or “comprehensive” surrender terms on August 2, 1943 (see <hi
                        rendition="#italic">post</hi>, <ref target="#pg537">p. 537</ref>, fn. 1),
                    the British draft available to Roosevelt at Birch Island on that date was that
                    annexed to C.C.S. 258, cited <hi
                        rendition="#italic">ante</hi>, <ref target="#pg525">p. 525</ref>, fn. 2.</p>
            </note>
            <note corresp="#d248-f2" n="2" xml:id="d248-f2-content">
                <p>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">Ante</hi>, <ref target="#pg519">pp. 519</ref>, <ref
                        target="#pg522">522</ref>.</p>
            </note>
            <note corresp="#d248-f3" n="3" xml:id="d248-f3-content">
                <p>Roosevelt’s message to Churchill, based on this instruction, was dispatched by
                    the White House Map Room at Washington as Roosevelt’s telegram No. 339.</p>
            </note>
        </listAnnotation>
    </standOff>
